# /etc/default/pi-say -- what this machine's speaker needs.
#
# pi5-deck, wired: a UGREEN USB audio adapter (KTMicro, 12d1:0010), which ALSA
# names CARD=Audio. Card numbers move with the order things are plugged in;
# the name comes from the product and does not. The microphone is a different
# card with a different name (CARD=Device), so the two cannot be confused.
PI_SAY_DEVICE=plughw:CARD=Audio,DEV=0

# Nothing else. The three settings below this line exist for Bluetooth and are
# deliberately absent now:
#
#   PI_SAY_RATE / PI_SAY_CHANNELS  an A2DP sink runs at a fixed 48 kHz stereo,
#       and letting ALSA convert piper's 22050 Hz mono on the fly buzzed
#       audibly, so the cache had to hold pre-converted audio. A wired DAC
#       takes 22050 mono directly and there is nothing to convert.
#
#   PI_SAY_LEAD_MS  a Bluetooth speaker lets its amp sleep between streams and
#       took about a second to come back, eating the start of every phrase --
#       which on a confirmation is the half that says what was understood. 1800
#       ms of silence was padded into every cached file to cover it. Wired, the
#       first syllable is there, and every reply is 1.8 s earlier.
